{{Quote box|width=30%|align=right|quote="I was eight songs into finishing the record, doing a vocal, and I heard the melody in my head before it was written. I couldn't tell if it was a song on the radio that I had heard or if it was a song my friend wrote or something. I picked up a guitar and it was kind of creepy, because the song was almost already written by itself. Within five minutes, the lyrics and everything else were finished. We tracked it the next week and it ended up being the first single. It was funny, because I felt there was another song that needed to be written during the project that was more upbeat and less moody."|source=—Wade talking about the development of "Hanging by a Moment".<ref name="Song Development">{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/bands/archive/l/lifehouse01/index2.jhtml#hanging|title=Lifehouse: Living The Moment (Making "Hanging by a Moment")|work=[[MTV]]|access-date=August 9, 2011|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121107180058/http://www.mtv.com/bands/archive/l/lifehouse01/index2.jhtml|archive-date=November 7, 2012}}</ref>}}
The song "Hanging by a Moment" was written by Lifehouse lead singer [[Jason Wade]].<ref name="Writing Credits">{{cite web|url={{AllMusic|class=album|id=r505749|pure_url=yes}}|title=No Name Face – Lifehouse|publisher=[[Rovi Corporation]]|access-date=August 2, 2011}}</ref>  It was produced by American record producer [[Ron Aniello]] and was mixed by [[Brendan O'Brien (record producer)|Brendan O'Brien]].<ref name="Production Credits">{{cite web|url=http://www.discogs.com/Lifehouse-No-Name-Face/release/1878943|title=Lifehouse – No Name Face (CD, Album) at Discogs|publisher=[[Discogs]]|access-date=August 2, 2011}}</ref> When asked about the song in an interview with [[Billboard (magazine)|''Billboard'']], Wade said, "It was the most uptempo, radio-friendly song. We all decided it was the right choice to release it as the first single." He went on to describe his expectations when writing songs, saying, "My ultimate goal in writing songs is to connect with people. In the lyrics, you don't tell the whole picture: You give a road to start on that people can relate to. We're honest, nice guys and I hope that comes across in everything we do."<ref name="Billboard Interview">{{cite magazine|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=TxEEAAAAMBAJ&q=lifehouse+hanging+by+a+moment&pg=PA11|title=Thanks To 1st Single, Lifehouse's 'Moment' Comes On Dreamworks|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|publisher=[[Nielsen Business Media]]|date=December 23, 2000|access-date=July 22, 2011|volume=112|issue=52|page=11}}</ref> After being asked how he wrote the song in an interview with [[LAUNCH (magazine)|''Launch'']], Wade explained, "I wrote that song without thinking about what was gonna happen to it and then it just kinda took over from there." He also said in the interview that he wrote "Hanging by a Moment" in about five minutes.<ref>[[#Juz06|Juzwiak 2006]]: 21</ref>

"Hanging by a Moment" was described as a [[post-grunge]] and [[alternative rock]] song that contains a strong melody.<ref name="Genre">{{cite web|url=http://new.music.yahoo.com/lifehouse/albums/hanging-by-a-moment-uk-cd--199417646|archive-url=https://archive.today/20130105112444/http://new.music.yahoo.com/lifehouse/albums/hanging-by-a-moment-uk-cd--199417646|url-status=dead|archive-date=January 5, 2013|title=Hanging by a Moment (UK CD) by Lifehouse|publisher=[[Yahoo! Music]]|access-date=August 2, 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|URL=https://numetalagenda.com/feature/the-15-greatest-and-10-worst-post-grunge-songs-of-all-time/|title=The 15 Greatest (and 10 Worst) Post-Grunge Songs of All Time|date=April 11, 2024|website=Nu Metal Agenda|access-date=December 26, 2025}}</ref> According to the sheet music published at Musicnotes.com by [[Sony/ATV Music Publishing]], the song is set in [[common time]] with a "moderate [[Rock music|rock]]" tempo of 124 [[beats per minute]].<ref name="Composition">{{cite web|url=http://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtdFPE.asp?ppn=MN0064818&mnuid%3DN0N2H0XC96Q44FL9VUKQZ3P2T2JVB1W7100NC1W7|title=Lifehouse – Hanging By a Moment Guitar Tab (Digital Download)|access-date=August 2, 2011|publisher=[[Sony/ATV Music Publishing]]}}</ref> It is composed in the key of [[D-flat major]].<ref>{{Cite web|last1=Jason|first1=Wade|last2=Lifehouse|date=May 25, 2009|title=Hanging By a Moment|url=https://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtd.asp?ppn=MN0074543|access-date=April 21, 2021|website=Musicnotes.com}}</ref> In an interview with ''Billboard'', lead singer and guitarist of Lifehouse, Jason Wade, described the song as an "uptempo, radio-friendly song".<ref name="BillboardArticle">{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/bbcom/news/article_display.jsp?vnu_content_id=1314580&inp=true#/bbcom/news/article_display.jsp?vnu_content_id=1314580&inp=true|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121111084629/http://www.billboard.com/bbcom/news/article_display.jsp?vnu_content_id=1314580&inp=true#/bbcom/news/article_display.jsp?vnu_content_id=1314580&inp=true|url-status=dead|archive-date=November 11, 2012|title=Lifehouse's 'Moment' Comes | magazine=Billboard|publisher=Nielsen Business Media|access-date=July 31, 2009}}</ref> Bill Lamb of [[About.com]] called the song "one of the biggest rock hits ever by a [[Contemporary Christian music|Contemporary Christian]] band crossing over into the mainstream. The song was the biggest hit of summer 2001 and was eventually named the most played song of the year on the radio."<ref name="About.com Article">{{cite web|url=http://top40.about.com/od/top10lists/tp/top10summer2001.htm|title=Top 10 Pop Songs – Summer 2001|last=Lamb|first=Bill|publisher=[[The New York Times Company]]|access-date=July 30, 2009|archive-date=June 5, 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110605001143/http://top40.about.com/od/top10lists/tp/top10summer2001.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref> Sean Rizzo of ''[[Sputnikmusic]]'' says that the song "presents one of the best with the guitar's plucking during the verses and a chorus infectious enough to infiltrate your brain for a few days."<ref name="SputnikMusicArticle">{{cite web|url=http://www.sputnikmusic.com/album.php?albumid=25024|title=Lifehouse – No Name Face Review – sputnikmusic|last=Rizzo|first=Sean|publisher=Sputnikmusic|access-date=July 30, 2009}}</ref> In a 2017 interview with ''Billboard'' on the core theme of the song, Wade said,  "I didn't really think about it when I was writing it. I knew at the end of it that it was a love song, and I kind of come from that world, so it can be interpreted as a spiritual song or a love song."<ref name="HBM-BILLBOARD-2017">{{cite web|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rock/lifehouse-hanging-by-a-moment-best-choruses-21st-century-jason-wade-interview-7775313/|title=Lifehouse's Jason Wade on How 'Hanging By A Moment' Came Together: 'It Was Like Lightning in a Bottle'|last=Weatherby|first=Taylor|publisher=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|access-date=March 19, 2019|date=April 27, 2017}}</ref>

